{\pard\sb360\sa120\keepn\b machine/ \u183? M0 to M6\par}
{\pard\sa160 The checks and the steps around them, as a Python package with one command, {\f1 mark1}. Everything it reads and writes is a file in this repository; there is no server and no database.\par}
{\pard\sb240\sa120\keepn\b How a run works\par}
{\pard\sa160 {\f1 mark1 check <paper>} (the author's self-check, A3) or {\f1 mark1 check <paper> --actor journal} (the journal's intake run) does this:\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 1.\tab Loads the record: {\f1 2-author/<paper>/} for the author, the submitted snapshot in {\f1 3-editor/<paper>/rounds/r<n>/record/} for the journal.\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 2.\tab Routes on the declared modality ({\f1 modality.py}, M2). Only formal theory is built.\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 3.\tab If the record has no AI appendix, runs the published generator ({\f1 generator.py}, M0).\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 4.\tab Runs the checks in {\f1 checks/} and {\f1 sieve/} (M1, M3, M4) and writes the findings report ({\f1 findings.py}, M5) and the evidence map ({\f1 sieve/contribution.py}, M6).\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 5.\tab On the journal side, marks every finding the author's own report lacks ({\f1 compare.py}).\par}
